   "text": "I read the structure region by region and used the sequence name printed under it (H\u2011Cpa\u2011cyclo[D\u2011Cys\u2011Tyr\u2011D\u2011Aph(Lys)\u2011Lys\u2011Thr\u2011Cys]\u2011D\u2011Tyr\u2011NH2) to assign most stereocentres. I did not verify each wedge against the name, except for Cpa.\n\n- **N\u2011terminus:** 4\u2011chlorophenylalanine (Cpa) with a free NH2. The hashed NH2 bond at its \u03b1\u2011carbon works out as S, so it is L\u2011Cpa.\n- **Macrocycle:** a disulfide bridge links the D\u2011Cys and Cys side chains. The residues run D\u2011Cys, Tyr, D\u2011Aph, Lys, Thr, Cys.\n- **D\u2011Aph(Lys):** a 4\u2011aminophenylalanine whose aniline nitrogen is acylated by L\u2011Lys. The Lys side chain is (CH2)4NH2 and its \u03b1\u2011amine is free.\n- **Ring Lys and Thr:** both have L configuration. The Thr side chain is CH(CH3)OH.\n- **C\u2011terminus:** D\u2011Tyr as the primary amide (C(N)=O), attached to the ring Cys carbonyl.\n\nThe SMILES uses ring label %10 for the disulfide and has not been run through a parser.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(Cl)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc(NC(=O)[C@@H](N)CCCCN)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(N)=O"
